msgid ""
"The unified format DID method selected is did:web, a method to retrieve DID "
"Documents via existing web (https) infrastructure​. ​The did:web identifiers"
" have the form ​. Resolution is accomplished by https GET against the URL "
"which is formed from this identifier by​ . For example "
"did:web:example.com:my:path would resolve a DID Document from the URL ​. "
"Additional did methods may be supported in the future."
msgstr ""
"所选的统一格式DID方法为did:web，这是一种通过现有web（https）基础设施检索DID文档的方法​。​did:web标识符的形式为​。解析通过对由该标识符经​"
"  形成的URL发出https GET请求来完成。例如，did:web:example.com:my:path将从URL​  "
"解析DID文档。今后可能支持其他DID方法。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_did_v1.md#L5
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_did_v1.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/concepts_did_v1.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_did_v1.md:5
msgid ""
"The unified format is based on the Decentralized Identifiers (DIDs) v1.0 "
"specification. DIDs are globally unique identifier in the form of URIs. The "
"URI scheme includes a method name which corresponds to a standard method by "
"which a DID Document can be resolved. This DID Document is a structured "
"JSON-LD which captures each existing public key (regardless of X.509 or JWK "
"format used) by the members of a trust network in a common format. It allows"
" additional metadata (such as intended purpose and key identifiers) to be "
"added to existing keys with changing the underlying keys themselves​. It "
"provides means to publish and cryptographically sign a master lists of keys "
"recognized used by a trust network."
msgstr ""
"统一格式基于去中心化标识符（DID）v1.0规范。DID是采用URI形式的全球唯一标识符。URI方案包含一个方法名称，对应于可据以解析DID文档的标准方法。该DID文档是一种结构化JSON-"
"LD，以通用格式记录信任网络成员的每个现有公钥（无论使用X.509格式还是JWK格式）。它允许在不改变底层密钥本身的情况下，为现有密钥添加附加元数据（例如预期用途和密钥标识符）​。它提供了发布信任网络所认可和使用的密钥主列表并对其进行加密签名的方法。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/concepts_did_v1.md#L14
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_did_v1.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/concepts_did_v1.html
#: input/pagecontent/concepts_did_v1.md:14
