#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/decision_support.html
#: input/pagecontent/decision_support.md:8
msgid ""
"Applying business rules in the context of trust networks for health "
"credentials requires a computable and standards-based approach for defining "
"the rules and subsequently evaluating them against credentials. For example,"
" individuals who wish to test their vaccine credentials against border entry"
" requirement prior to travel must be able to evaluate the business rules for"
" a variety of destination jurisdictions against a variety of credential "
"formats."
msgstr ""
"在健康凭证信任网络的背景下应用业务规则，需要采用一种可计算且基于标准的方法来定义规则，并随后针对凭证对规则进行评估。例如，希望在旅行前根据边境入境要求检验其疫苗凭证的个人，必须能够针对多种凭证格式评估多个目的地管辖区的业务规则。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/decision_support.md#L389
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/decision_support.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/decision_support.html
#: input/pagecontent/decision_support.md:389
msgid ""
"As an alternative to translating the CQL, if the desired CQL already exists "
"and the ELM translation is packaged with the CQL as part of a FHIR Library "
"then the ELM can be extracted from the Library. This document describes how "
"to extract the ELM using a simple Node.js project. Node.js will first need "
"to be installed if it is not already available. A new Node.js project can be"
" set up using npm:"
msgstr ""
"作为翻译CQL的替代方案，如果所需的CQL已经存在，且其ELM翻译作为FHIR "
"Library的一部分与CQL一起打包，则可从该Library中提取ELM。本文档介绍如何使用一个简单的Node.js项目提取ELM。如尚未安装Node.js，需先行安装。可使用npm建立新的Node.js项目："

