#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L9
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:9
msgid ""
"A good starting point is to identify how the use of a digital solution can "
"contribute to important general duties of any government through public "
"health. Three key objectives of public health action are:"
msgstr "一个良好的起点是确定数字解决方案的使用如何能够通过公共卫生，促进任何政府均承担的重要一般性职责。公共卫生行动的三项关键目标是："

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L46
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:46
msgid ""
"A number of further possible uses for digital PHRs raise ethical issues. In "
"the context of a public health emergency, a digital PHR might play a role in"
" achieving various public health purposes such as determining vaccination "
"coverage in a given population, which may help to determine when to lift or "
"relax public health and social measures (PHSMs) at a population level. A "
"digital PHR might also be used to facilitate individualized exemption from, "
"or, reduction of PHSMs (e.g. reduced quarantine time post exposure) or "
"individual access to an activity based on proof of vaccination (if such uses"
" are held to be ethical), which we can term a “health pass” function. The "
"potential deployment or utilization of a digital PHR for these purposes, "
"particularly as a health pass, engenders a number of potential ethical "
"problems for individuals and communities, and human rights challenges (3,4)."
msgstr ""
"数字个人健康记录（PHR）的其他若干可能用途也引发了伦理问题。在突发公共卫生事件背景下，数字PHR可能在实现各种公共卫生目的方面发挥作用，例如确定特定人群的疫苗接种覆盖率，这可能有助于确定何时在人群层面解除或放宽公共卫生和社会措施（PHSM）。数字PHR还可能用于便利个人豁免或减少PHSM（例如缩短接触后的检疫时间），或基于疫苗接种证明使个人得以参与某项活动（如果此类用途被认为符合伦理），我们可将其称为“健康通行证”功能。为上述目的部署或使用数字PHR，特别是作为健康通行证，会给个人和社区带来若干潜在的伦理问题以及人权挑战（3,4）。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L90
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:90
msgid "ALL COMMUNICATION SHOULD BE CLEAR AND TRANSPARENT."
msgstr "所有沟通均宜清晰、透明。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L83
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:83
msgid ""
"ALL NECESSARY MEASURES SHOULD BE PUT IN PLACE TO PROTECT PARTICIPANTS FOR "
"CONTINUITY OF CARE.  A digital solution will include potentially sensitive "
"data relating to the health of individuals, and this data should therefore "
"be protected by appropriate medical confidentiality and privacy safeguards. "
"Access to or use of the data for continuity of care should be based on the "
"appropriate consent standard (e.g. implied or explicit) in a given health-"
"care system and should be sufficient for the receiving health-care provider "
"or team to continue providing good medical care. These ethical standards "
"will also apply to international transfer of  data for continuity of care "
"(such as when a patient accesses medical services abroad)."
msgstr ""
"宜采取一切必要措施，为保障医疗连续性而保护参与者。数字解决方案将包含与个人健康相关的潜在敏感数据，因此这些数据宜受到适当的医疗保密和隐私保障措施的保护。为医疗连续性而访问或使用这些数据，宜以特定卫生保健系统中适当的同意标准（例如默示同意或明示同意）为依据，并宜足以使接收方卫生保健提供者或团队继续提供良好的医疗服务。这些伦理标准也将适用于为医疗连续性而进行的数据国际传输（例如患者在国外获得医疗服务时）。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L23
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:23
msgid ""
"Another example of working towards objective 2 is to think about ways to try"
" and achieve equity through the distribution of health resources. While a "
"digital solution may offer a more reliable, accurate and trusted mechanism "
"to record an personal health history, they risk exacerbating health "
"inequities, for the following reasons."
msgstr ""
"努力实现目标2的另一个例子是，思考如何通过卫生资源的分配来努力实现公平。虽然数字解决方案可以提供一种更可靠、更准确、更可信的机制来记录个人健康史，但由于以下原因，它们有可能加剧卫生不公平。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L119
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:119
msgid ""
"Any retention of personal data processed in the interest of the application "
"of the digital solution should have a legitimate and fair basis. Before any "
"data are retained, the potential risks, harms and benefits should be "
"considered. Personal data should be permanently deleted after the time "
"needed to fulfil their purpose, unless their extended retention is justified"
" for specified purposes."
msgstr ""
"为应用数字解决方案而处理的个人数据，任何保留均宜具有合法、公平的依据。在保留任何数据之前，宜考虑潜在的风险、危害和益处。个人数据在其实现目的所需的时间届满后宜予以永久删除，除非为特定目的延长保留是合理的。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L148
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:148
msgid ""
"CONFIDENTIALITY AND SECURITY  Personal data processed in the interest of the"
" application of the digital solution should be kept confidential and not "
"disclosed to unauthorized parties; personal data should only be accessible "
"to the data subject or to other explicitly authorized parties."
msgstr "保密和安全 为应用数字解决方案而处理的个人数据宜予以保密，不向未经授权的各方披露；个人数据宜仅可由数据主体或其他经明确授权的各方访问。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L105
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:105
msgid "Data protection principles for a Digital Solution"
msgstr "数字解决方案的数据保护原则"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L161
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:161
msgid ""
"DATA SUBJECT RIGHTS, COMPLAINT AND LEGAL REDRESS Data Holders, if they have "
"provided sufficient evidence of being the Data Holder, should be able to "
"exercise data subject rights. These data subject rights include the right of"
" access, correction, deletion, objection and restriction of personal data, "
"subject to conditions regulated by national law, decree, regulation or other"
" official act or order. Data subjects have the right to seek redress by a "
"complaint procedure if they suffer harm or loss as a result of misused  data"
" or incorrect or incomplete data. Data subjects should be provided with "
"easily accessible, concise, comprehensible and reader-friendly information "
"about how they might exercise their data subject rights and how to seek "
"legal redress, including how they can exercise any rights in the case of "
"alleged fraud."
msgstr ""
"数据主体权利、投诉和法律救济 "
"数据持有人如已提供充分证据证明其为数据持有人，宜能够行使数据主体权利。这些数据主体权利包括对个人数据的访问权、更正权、删除权、反对权和限制处理权，但须遵守国家法律、法令、条例或其他正式法令或命令所规定的条件。数据主体如因数据被滥用或数据不正确或不完整而遭受损害或损失，有权通过投诉程序寻求救济。宜向数据主体提供易于获取、简明、易懂且便于阅读的信息，说明其如何行使数据主体权利以及如何寻求法律救济，包括在涉嫌欺诈的情况下如何行使任何权利。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L145
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:145
msgid ""
"Data use should be monitored to ensure that it does not exceed the "
"legitimate use. Personal data retained in the interest of the application of"
" the digital solution should only be retained and stored for the time that "
"is necessary for specified purposes. Personal data accessed at the point of "
"verification of the digital solution should not be retained and stored in a "
"repository, database or otherwise."
msgstr ""
"宜对数据使用进行监测，确保其不超出合法用途。为应用数字解决方案而保留的个人数据，宜仅在特定目的所必需的时间内予以保留和存储。在验证数字解决方案时访问的个人数据，不宜在存储库、数据库或其他地方予以保留和存储。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L172
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:172
msgid "Digital personal health record design criteria"
msgstr "数字个人健康记录设计标准"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L188
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:188
msgid ""
"Digital technology should not be the only mechanism available for "
"verification. There should always be possible ways to revert to a paper-only"
" manual verification of records. It is important to note that despite the "
"technological design criteria outlined here, it will be essential for Member"
" States to ensure that the legal and policy frameworks are in place to "
"support responsible use of the digital solution as defined by the Member "
"State."
msgstr ""
"数字技术不宜成为唯一可用的验证机制。宜始终保留可以退回到仅基于纸质记录的人工验证的方式。需要指出的是，尽管本文概述了技术设计标准，但会员国务必确保建立相应的法律和政策框架，以支持按会员国所界定的方式负责任地使用数字解决方案。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L174
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:174
msgid ""
"Due to the ethical considerations and data protection principles outlined "
"above, the following design criteria were considered when formulating the "
"requirements for implementing a digital solution."
msgstr "鉴于上文概述的伦理考虑和数据保护原则，在制定实施数字解决方案的要求时考虑了以下设计标准。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L68
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:68
msgid ""
"Each Member State that introduces a digital solution should be clear about "
"which uses are proposed and that it should not be used for other purposes."
msgstr "每个引入数字解决方案的会员国均宜明确拟议的用途，并明确该解决方案不宜用于其他目的。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L44
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:44
msgid ""
"Ethical considerations related to further potential uses of digital personal"
" health records for public health security measures"
msgstr "与数字个人健康记录在公共卫生安全措施方面的其他潜在用途相关的伦理考虑"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L3
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:3
msgid ""
"Ethics should be an integral part of the design and deployment of a digital "
"solution. However, policy decisions are often complex and difficult. Many "
"different considerations will need to be made and weighed against each "
"other. Often, the evidence is uncertain and there are many different "
"competing ethical perspectives and positions. Evidence alone will not "
"provide the right answer, nor will a simple set of ethical rules. Public "
"health action requires careful judgement and acceptance of responsibility "
"for the outcomes. A number of different ethical considerations should be "
"taken into account, including both objectives and processes."
msgstr ""
"伦理宜成为数字解决方案设计和部署的组成部分。然而，政策决定往往复杂而困难。需要考虑并权衡许多不同的因素。证据往往不确定，并存在许多相互竞争的不同伦理观点和立场。仅靠证据无法提供正确答案，一套简单的伦理规则也无法做到。公共卫生行动需要审慎判断，并对结果承担责任。宜考虑若干不同的伦理因素，包括目标和过程两方面。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L48
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:48
msgid ""
"First, use of a digital PHR as a health pass raises a distinct set of risks "
"because of current scientific uncertainties emergent diseases.  For example,"
" during the COVID-19 Public Health Emergency of International Concern "
"(PHEIC), COVID-19 vaccines have demonstrated efficacy and effectiveness in "
"preventing severe disease and death, the extent to which each vaccine "
"prevents transmission of SARS-CoV-2 to susceptible individuals were not "
"fully assessed. How long each vaccine confers protection against severe "
"disease and against infection, and how well each protects against current "
"and future variants of SARS-CoV-2 were not fully known. In this context of "
"scientific uncertainty, use of a digital PHR as a health pass based solely "
"on individual vaccination status may increase the risk of disease spread. "
"This is particularly the case if individuals with a digital PHR are "
"completely exempted from PHSMs or if it is hard to enforce individuals’ "
"compliance with required"
msgstr ""
"首先，由于新发疾病当前存在科学上的不确定性，将数字PHR用作健康通行证会带来一系列特殊风险。例如，在COVID-19国际关注的突发公共卫生事件（PHEIC）期间，COVID-19疫苗已证明在预防重症和死亡方面具有效力和效果，但每种疫苗在多大程度上可防止SARS-"
"CoV-2传播给易感个体尚未得到充分评估。每种疫苗针对重症和感染的保护作用可持续多久，以及每种疫苗对SARS-"
"CoV-2当前和未来变异株的保护效果如何，当时尚未完全明了。在这种科学不确定的背景下，仅基于个人疫苗接种状况将数字PHR用作健康通行证，可能会增加疾病传播的风险。如果持有数字PHR的个人被完全豁免PHSM，或者难以强制要求个人遵守所要求的"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L87
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:87
msgid ""
"For adults without decisional capacity, use of their personal health records"
" for decisions relating to their health care may be based on their advance "
"decisions or, in the absence of an advance decision, be made in the adult’s "
"best interest by a health-care proxy or an authorized surrogate. Minors with"
" sufficient intelligence and maturity should be able to allow the use of "
"their health record data for continuity of care, where consent is required."
msgstr ""
"对于无决策能力的成年人，将其个人健康记录用于与其卫生保健相关的决策，可依据其预先决定；如无预先决定，可由卫生保健代理人或经授权的替代决策者以该成年人的最大利益为出发点作出。具有足够智力和成熟度的未成年人，在需要同意的情况下，宜能够允许为医疗连续性而使用其健康记录数据。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L95
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:95
msgid ""
"If, in the future, the uses of the solution are extended into other "
"scientific or public health purposes (e.g. programme monitoring or "
"research), data subjects and other members of the public should be informed "
"of the nature and occurrences of these activities in advance, the ethics "
"oversight or governance structure in place (including for surveillance "
"activities (7)), and options for controlling or limiting personal health "
"data for these uses. personal health data are sensitive and should, in "
"general, be anonymized (or pseudonymized, or de-identified) for scientific "
"or public health purposes, to minimize risks to the data subjects. Where "
"personal health data need to be retained in an identifiable form for these "
"purposes, consideration should be given to whether consent is required or "
"should be waived based on satisfaction of appropriate ethical criteria (e.g."
" minimal risk, impracticability of obtaining consent, no adverse effects on "
"the rights and welfare of the data subjects, and serving a public health "
"good)."
msgstr ""
"如果将来该解决方案的用途扩展到其他科学或公共卫生目的（例如规划监测或研究），宜事先告知数据主体和其他公众这些活动的性质和发生情况、现行的伦理监督或治理结构（包括针对监测活动的结构（7）），以及控制或限制将个人健康数据用于这些用途的选项。个人健康数据属于敏感数据，用于科学或公共卫生目的时一般宜进行匿名化（或假名化、去标识化）处理，以尽量减少对数据主体的风险。如果出于这些目的需要以可识别形式保留个人健康数据，宜考虑是否需要征得同意，或者在满足适当伦理标准（例如风险极小、获取同意不切实际、对数据主体的权利和福祉无不利影响，以及服务于公共卫生利益）的情况下是否宜免除同意。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L92
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:92
msgid ""
"Implementation details of a digital solution relevant to users should be "
"communicated in a transparent manner, which may contribute to the promotion "
"of public trust and acceptance of the solution. This communication includes "
"how the solution would work to benefit individuals and public health, the "
"policies and mechanisms in place to limit access to and use of the solution "
"by third parties, whether personal health data are linked to other types of "
"data and the purposes of any data linkage."
msgstr ""
"宜以透明的方式向用户传达与其相关的数字解决方案实施细节，这可能有助于增进公众对该解决方案的信任和接受。这种沟通包括：该解决方案将如何发挥作用以惠及个人和公共卫生；为限制第三方访问和使用该解决方案而制定的政策和机制；个人健康数据是否与其他类型的数据相关联；以及任何数据关联的目的。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L176
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:176
msgid ""
"Implementation of the digital solution should not increase health inequities"
" or increase the digital divide. Every individual in the jurisdiction should"
" have the right to obtain and hold records on a digital solution.  The "
"records held by the digital solution need to be in a format that can be "
"accessible to all, for example, in paper and digital formats. Any solution "
"should also work in online and offline environments across multiple "
"platforms – paper and digital. Individuals should not be treated differently"
" or given different levels of trust due to the representation format of the "
"data they are using (e.g. there should be no discrimination based on whether"
" someone is presenting a health record on a smartphone or a paper card). Any"
" solution should not be at an additional cost to the person. The "
"interoperability specifications used in digital solutions should be based on"
" open standards to ensure equitable access to a range of non-proprietary "
"digital tools. The infrastructure that the digital solution solution is "
"built on should ensure that individuals and Member States are not locked "
"into a commitment with only one vendor. Any solution should be as "
"environmentally friendly as possible. The most environmentally sustainable "
"options should be pursued to reduce any additional undue harm to the "
"environment. Any solution should be designed to augment and work within the "
"context of existing health information systems, as appropriate. Any solution"
" should not share or store more data than is needed to successfully execute "
"its tasks. Minimization of health content for purposes not related to health"
" care, and privacy-protecting features, should be built into the system and "
"be respected accordingly. Anti-fraud mechanisms should be built into any "
"approach."
msgstr ""
"数字解决方案的实施不宜加剧卫生不公平或扩大数字鸿沟。管辖范围内的每个人均宜有权在数字解决方案中获取和持有记录。数字解决方案所持有的记录须采用所有人均可获取的格式，例如纸质格式和数字格式。任何解决方案还宜能够在跨多个平台（纸质和数字）的在线和离线环境中运行。不宜因个人所使用数据的呈现格式而区别对待或给予不同程度的信任（例如，不宜因某人是在智能手机上还是在纸质卡片上出示健康记录而有所歧视）。任何解决方案均不宜给个人带来额外费用。数字解决方案中使用的互操作性规范宜基于开放标准，以确保公平获取一系列非专有数字工具。数字解决方案所依托的基础设施宜确保个人和会员国不会被锁定于仅与单一供应商的承诺。任何解决方案均宜尽可能环保。宜采用环境可持续性最高的选项，以减少对环境的任何额外不当危害。任何解决方案均宜酌情设计为在现有卫生信息系统的背景下进行补充和运行。任何解决方案共享或存储的数据均不宜超出成功执行其任务所需的数据。宜在系统中内置针对与卫生保健无关目的的健康内容最小化功能以及隐私保护功能，并予以相应遵守。任何方法均宜内置防欺诈机制。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L157
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:157
msgid ""
"In case of a security breach leading to the accidental or unlawful "
"destruction, loss, alteration, unauthorized disclosure of or access to "
"personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed, users of the "
"digital solution,n that hold health records (Data Holders) should be "
"notified in an appropriate and timely manner.  Data Holders should be "
"notified of: any data breach; the nature of the data breach, which may "
"affect their rights as data subjects; and recommendations to mitigate "
"potential adverse effects."
msgstr ""
"如发生安全漏洞，导致所传输、存储或以其他方式处理的个人数据意外或非法地被破坏、丢失、篡改、未经授权披露或访问，宜以适当、及时的方式通知持有健康记录的数字解决方案用户（数据持有人）。宜向数据持有人通知：任何数据泄露；可能影响其作为数据主体之权利的数据泄露的性质；以及减轻潜在不利影响的建议。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L20
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:20
msgid ""
"In relation to objective 2, equal treatment requires respecting and "
"protecting all persons equally and acting to ensure, as far as possible, "
"that there is no discrimination against anyone. An example of how to work "
"towards this objective is to ensure that appropriate personal data "
"protection safeguards are implemented. Individual health data is private "
"information, and protections need to be in place to ensure that no "
"individual is forced to disclose or publicly display their personal health "
"record (PHR) to access any public area or activity (1). Such a practice "
"and/or the lack of a PHR itself may result in the stigmatization of "
"individuals without a PHR and may exacerbate the risk of harms."
msgstr ""
"关于目标2，平等对待要求平等地尊重和保护所有人，并采取行动尽可能确保不对任何人有所歧视。努力实现这一目标的一个例子是确保实施适当的个人数据保护保障措施。个人健康数据属于私人信息，需要采取保护措施，确保任何个人都不会被迫披露或公开展示其个人健康记录（PHR）才能进入任何公共区域或参与任何公共活动（1）。此类做法和/或缺乏PHR本身，可能导致没有PHR的个人受到污名化，并可能加剧受到伤害的风险。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L30
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:30
msgid ""
"In relation to objective 3, trust is vital to ensuring the benefits of a "
"digital solution for individuals, communities and the whole population. For "
"example, the provision of robust data protection measures and the use of "
"procedural considerations, outlined in section 1.3.4, may contribute to the "
"maintenance of trust in public health systems. This in turn contributes to "
"the delivery of objective 1. Another example might be that a digital "
"solution should only be used for its intended purpose, as inappropriate uses"
" may result in legitimate ones being undermined."
msgstr ""
"关于目标3，信任对于确保数字解决方案惠及个人、社区和全体人口至关重要。例如，提供强有力的数据保护措施以及采用第1.3.4节所述的程序性考虑，可能有助于维护对公共卫生系统的信任。这反过来又有助于实现目标1。另一个例子可能是，数字解决方案宜仅用于其预期目的，因为不当用途可能导致合法用途受到损害。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L166
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:166
msgid ""
"INDEPENDENT OVERSIGHT AND ACCOUNTABILITY  An independent public authority "
"should be responsible for monitoring whether any data controller and data "
"processor involved in the processing of personal data in the interest of the"
" digital solution adhere to the principles, and may recommend revoking the "
"authorization to collect or otherwise process  data. Such a public authority"
" should have access to all information necessary to fulfil its task. "
"Adequate policies and mechanisms should be in place to ensure adherence to "
"these principles."
msgstr ""
"独立监督和问责 "
"宜由一个独立的公共当局负责监测参与为数字解决方案而处理个人数据的任何数据控制者和数据处理者是否遵守这些原则，并可建议撤销其收集或以其他方式处理数据的授权。该公共当局宜能够获取履行其任务所需的一切信息。宜制定适当的政策和机制，确保这些原则得到遵守。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L1
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:1
msgid "Key ethical considerations"
msgstr "关键伦理考虑"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L7
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:7
msgid "Objectives"
msgstr "目标"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L78
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:78
msgid ""
"OBTAINING AND USING A DIGITAL SOLUTION SHOULD BE AS INCLUSIVE AND FAIR AS "
"POSSIBLE.   Digital solutions should be as inclusive as possible and should "
"not create disadvantage. To achieve this, it may be necessary to provide "
"alternative, cost-effective  solutions, including paper-based alternatives, "
"for individuals and groups with existing disadvantages, such as those with "
"digital skill or disability barriers, those living in areas with poorer "
"digital connectivity, and undocumented or irregular migrants. No one should "
"be excluded through a requirement for individual payment to obtain and use a"
" digital solution."
msgstr ""
"获取和使用数字解决方案宜尽可能具有包容性和公平性。数字解决方案宜尽可能具有包容性，不宜造成不利处境。为此，可能需要为已处于不利处境的个人和群体提供具有成本效益的替代解决方案，包括纸质替代方案；这些个人和群体例如存在数字技能或残疾障碍者、生活在数字连接较差地区者，以及无证或非正常移民。任何人都不宜因需要个人付费才能获取和使用数字解决方案而被排除在外。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L117
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:117
msgid ""
"Personal data collected for the application of the digital solution should "
"only be accessed, analysed or otherwise used while respecting the legitimate"
" interests of the data subjects concerned. Specifically, to ensure that data"
" use is fair, data should not be used in a way that violates human rights or"
" in any other ways that are likely to cause unjustified or adverse effects "
"on any individual(s) or group(s) of individuals."
msgstr ""
"为应用数字解决方案而收集的个人数据，宜仅在尊重相关数据主体合法利益的前提下进行访问、分析或以其他方式使用。具体而言，为确保数据使用公平，使用数据的方式不宜侵犯人权，也不宜以任何其他可能对任何个人或个人群体造成不合理或不利影响的方式使用数据。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L136
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:136
msgid ""
"Personal data processed in the interest of the application of the digital "
"solution should be relevant to the purposes for which they are to be used "
"and, to the extent necessary for those purposes, be accurate, complete, and "
"kept up to date."
msgstr "为应用数字解决方案而处理的个人数据宜与其拟用于的目的相关，并在这些目的所必需的范围内做到准确、完整和及时更新。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L50
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:50
msgid ""
"PHSMs during an activity (e.g. mask wearing and physical distancing during a"
" concert) to which they are allowed access based on their digital PHR."
msgstr "PHSM（例如在音乐会期间佩戴口罩和保持身体距离），而这些个人是依据其数字PHR获准参加该活动的，则情况尤其如此。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L74
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:74
msgid ""
"POTENTIAL BENEFITS, RISKS AND COSTS SHOULD BE ASSESSED BEFORE INTRODUCTION "
"OF A DIGITAL SOLUTION."
msgstr "在引入数字解决方案之前，宜评估其潜在益处、风险和成本。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L32
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:32
msgid "Processes"
msgstr "过程"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L139
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:139
msgid ""
"PROPORTIONALITY, NECESSITY AND DATA MINIMIZATION The processing of personal "
"data should be relevant (have a rational link to specified purposes), "
"adequate (sufficient to properly fulfil the specified purposes) and limited "
"to what is required to fulfil the specified purposes. The processing of "
"personal data should not be excessive for the"
msgstr ""
"相称性、必要性和数据最小化 "
"个人数据的处理宜具有相关性（与特定目的存在合理联系）、充分性（足以妥善实现特定目的），并限于实现特定目的所需的范围。个人数据的处理不宜超出"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L128
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:128
msgid ""
"PURPOSE LIMITATION AND SPECIFICATION  As the personal data collected in the "
"interest of the digital solution may only be used for the scope and purpose "
"identified, and they should not be processed in ways that are incompatible "
"with identified purposes. The use of  data for any other purpose, including "
"the sale and use of personal data for commercial purposes, should be "
"prohibited, except with the explicit, unambiguous and freely given prior "
"consent of the data subject."
msgstr ""
"目的限定和明确 "
"为数字解决方案而收集的个人数据只能用于既定的范围和目的，不宜以与既定目的不相符的方式进行处理。宜禁止将数据用于任何其他目的，包括出售个人数据和将个人数据用于商业目的，除非事先获得数据主体明确、无歧义且自由给予的同意。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L143
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:143
msgid ""
"purposes for which those personal data are collected. Data collected and "
"retained on the digital solution should be as limited as possible, "
"respecting proportionality and necessity. Data access, analysis or other use"
" should be kept to the minimum necessary to fulfil their purpose. The amount"
" of data, including their granularity, should be limited to the minimum "
"necessary. Selective disclosure mechanisms should be used to support "
"proportionate data access."
msgstr ""
"收集这些个人数据的目的。在数字解决方案中收集和保留的数据宜尽可能有限，遵循相称性和必要性原则。数据的访问、分析或其他使用宜保持在实现其目的所需的最低限度。数据量（包括其粒度）宜限于必要的最低限度。宜采用选择性披露机制，以支持相称的数据访问。"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L62
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:62
msgid "Recommendations"
msgstr "建议"

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-
#. trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md#L191
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/ethical_principles.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/ethical_principles.html
#: input/pagecontent/ethical_principles.md:191
